typhoon patch on fm1-base: USB audio per direction, off / mute / on at a level, the recording's source
SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0 (a change to fm1-base's MPL-2.0 files)

What: plat_usb_audio_set(rec, rec_q12, play, play_q12, from) (include/plat.h). Each direction USB_AUDIO_OFF (not
presented: felucca-bsp's usb_audio_switch, patches/felucca-bsp/0001), USB_AUDIO_MUTE (a level of 0) or
USB_AUDIO_ON at its level, 0 .. 200 %; the recording either the mix (the playback in it) or the app alone. Once an
app calls it the render runs at full level (as plat_usb_audio_full), the recording takes a scaled, saturated copy
(device/main_fm1.c rec_tap, 2 KB in the pool), the playback is mixed at its own level, MASTER is the speaker's and
the headphones' only, and the speaker's mix saturates. Without the call, nothing changes. The host simulator keeps
what was asked (host_usb_audio) and renders as the FM-1 then does.
Why: typhoon's USB AUDIO page (each direction OFF / MUTE / ON, its level; the recording MIX or SYNTH).
Applies to: fm1-base 934e40d. Needs patches/felucca-bsp/0001.
Upstream: not offered yet (charlesvestal/fm1-base).

diff --git a/device/main_fm1.c b/device/main_fm1.c
index ecac760..e65f3ad 100644
--- a/device/main_fm1.c
+++ b/device/main_fm1.c
@@ -31,6 +31,21 @@ static uint32_t wdt_stage __attribute__((section(".noinit")));   /* the main loo
                                                                   * 2 Bluetooth, 3 the app's loop, 4 USB, 5 a frame,
                                                                   * 6 input (fm1b_dbg.stage) */
 
+#if FELUCCA_UAC
+/* the recording at its own level (plat_usb_audio_set): from a copy, so the speaker's is untouched; saturated */
+static int32_t rec_blk[2u * REND_FRAMES] PLAT_POOL;
+static void rec_tap(const int32_t *o)
+{
+    const float g = (float)uac_rec_q12 * (1.0f / 4096.0f);
+    uint32_t i;
+    for (i = 0; i < 2u * REND_FRAMES; i++) {
+        const float v = (float)o[i] * g;
+        rec_blk[i] = v > 8388607.0f ? 8388607 : v < -8388607.0f ? -8388607 : (int32_t)v;
+    }
+    uac_tap(rec_blk, REND_FRAMES);
+}
+#endif
+
